{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## LIVE VALIDATION SATISFIED — observed through the deployed server\n\nChange 2275 merged and deployed; the running container is `rebar-mcp-97b003c4cd0e-8093`\n(`97b003c4cd0e` = the ref-root fix).\n\n**Call made** — `tools/call` -> `review_plan` with `{\"ticket_id\": \"1eb6-65f2-5a4e-4c7b\"}`,\nauthenticated, against `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`.\n\n**Result — the reported failure is GONE:**\n\n    cannot resolve ref     present=False     <-- the defect this ticket is about\n    llm_unavailable        present=True\n    bedrock                present=True\n    verdict                present=True\n\nThe response is a real `plan_review_verdict` (`INDETERMINATE` with populated `advisory`\nfindings, e.g. 'vague/subjective terms present'), not a snapshot error. The deterministic floor\nran against a resolved tree.\n\n**Why this is the discriminating evidence and not merely 'no longer erroring'.** The failure did\nnot disappear into a pass; it MOVED to a different, independently-tracked cause. `origin/main`\nnow resolves — so the snapshot layer is reading `REBAR_ROOT`'s checkout — and what remains is\n`facial-lunar-urson`: the container is built `--extra agents --extra mcp` while `[agents]`\ndeclares `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic,retries,duckduckgo]` with NO bedrock, and `[bedrock]` is a\nseparate extra. Two different defects; only one of them was this ticket's.\n\n**One negative check worth recording.** I first ran `plan_review_status` and got a clean\nstructured verdict, and nearly cited it as validation. It would not have been: that tool is\ndocumented as a purely LOCAL check with no LLM and no network, so it never touches the snapshot\nlayer and could not have exercised the fix. The evidence had to come from a tool that actually\nresolves a ref.\n\nEarlier in this ticket I claimed 2271 had fixed the gates without validating through the\ndeployed server, and was wrong. This time the claim rests on an observed call and its response."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787868151892744001,"uuid":"b452101e-17c6-4b94-b58e-711ed75f4973"}